."],"a":0,"p":"674","k":"Selective estrogen receptor modulators"},{"s":"A woman on tamoxifen for ER-positive breast cancer has postmenopausal bleeding. Why?","o":["Tamoxifen is an antagonist at the uterus","Tamoxifen blocks progesterone","Tamoxifen causes thrombocytopenia","Tamoxifen causes vaginal atrophy only","Tamoxifen is a partial agonist at the uterus, causing endometrial hyperplasia or cancer"],"e":["Wrong. Partial agonist.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not the cause.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"674","k":"Selective estrogen receptor modulators"},{"s":"A postmenopausal woman with osteoporosis wants a SERM that does not raise her endometrial cancer risk. Which drug fits?","o":["Raloxifene","Anastrozole","Tamoxifen","Ethinyl estradiol","Clomiphene"],"e":["Correct. Antagonist at breast and uterus, agonist at bone.","Wrong. Not a SERM.","Wrong. Endometrial agonist.","Wrong. Not a SERM.","Wrong. Infertility."],"a":0,"p":"674","k":"Selective estrogen receptor modulators"},{"s":"Which serious adverse effect is shared by tamoxifen and raloxifene?","o":["Hyperkalemia","Thromboembolic events, especially in smokers","Hepatic adenoma","Osteoporosis","Endometrial cancer"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Both protect bone.","Wrong. Tamoxifen only."],"a":1,"p":"674","k":"Selective estrogen receptor modulators"},{"s":"Tamoxifen is also used in men to prevent:","o":["Infertility","Gynecomastia during prostate cancer therapy","Prostate enlargement","Erectile dysfunction","Testicular atrophy"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"674","k":"Selective estrogen receptor modulators"},{"s":"A postmenopausal woman with ER-positive breast cancer starts anastrozole. How does it work?","o":["Inhibits peripheral conversion of androgens to estrogen","Blocks GnRH","Inhibits 5α-reductase","Blocks progesterone receptors","Blocks estrogen receptors in breast"],"